1"],["heading","HOW TO READ THE DIAGRAM"],["text","1. Counting sort counts each key: for [3,1,3,2], counts for 0..3 are [0,1,1,2]."],["text","2. Emit each key according to its count: [1,2,3,3]."],["text","3. Heap sort builds a max heap, swaps the root with the last unsorted cell, and restores the\nheap repeatedly."],["heading","INTERVIEW MEMORY TIP"],["text","Counting sort costs O(n+k) for bounded integer range k; heap sort costs O(n log n)."]]